  "original_full_abstract": "We specify six algebraic boundary points, an incoming center, and at least five distinct outgoing centers for a cube move of 16-realizations. Existence follows from strict rational sign bounds for two continuous one-variable residuals. The boundary parameters are uniquely defined real roots of monotone polynomials. This contradicts the at-most-three expectation for construction curves sharing a focus in Remark 4.8 of Melotti–Ramassamy–Thévenin, in the realization setting allowing crossings. The fixed boundary is crossed, so the example concerns no proper embedding. Neither the exact number of centers for this boundary nor a universal maximum is determined.",
  "original_publication_date": "2026-10-15",
  "native_version_field_present": false,
  "native_version": null,
  "printed_version_field_present": false,
  "printed_version": null,
  "no_version_field_to_be_synthesized_in_Bib_JSONLD_or_citation_metadata": true,
  "full_original_result": "One fixed distinct six-point algebraic crossed boundary, both alternating triples noncollinear, one actual incoming center and at least five distinct outgoing centers at alpha16; all six ordered faces; two distinct individually smooth common-focus curves and A3 witness.",
  "scope_limits": "At least five, no exact total/global maximum/proper embedding/alpha below one/joint transversality/firstness/current worldwide openness. MRT Remark4.8 and OWR crossing-permitted maximum-three target, not separate existence theorem.",
  "classical_credits_and_editions_preserved": "Ash–Bolker weighted and pure fourth-power family vs separate oscillatory example; BPR actualv2 Definition4.12 and BR actualv1 Section1.7; selected root body scope and immutable peer access limits retained, later finalBR not newly read.",
